WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.659 --> 00:00:05.399
Over the years, Marvel has populated its sprawling
cinematic universe with an extraordinarily

00:00:05.399 --> 00:00:09.710
talented cast of actors and actresses, but
the studio has still never quite been able

00:00:09.710 --> 00:00:11.620
to grab Keanu Reeves for a role.

00:00:11.620 --> 00:00:13.450
And that's not for lack of trying, either.

00:00:13.450 --> 00:00:16.680
So just why hasn't Reeves shown up in the
MCU so far?

00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:22.260
Everyone knows Marvel likes to lock lead actors
into hefty multi-picture deals, such as Chadwick

00:00:22.269 --> 00:00:27.210
Boseman's reported five-film contract and
Sebastian Stan's whopping nine-movie deal.

00:00:27.210 --> 00:00:31.539
And while signing a Marvel movie contract
comes with many, many perks, there's no denying

00:00:31.539 --> 00:00:35.370
that agreeing to film half a dozen movies
over the course of a few years definitely

00:00:35.370 --> 00:00:38.649
cuts down on the number of other projects
an actor can take on.

00:00:38.649 --> 00:00:42.830
Other actors like John Krasinski and Emily
Blunt have previously discussed the projects

00:00:42.830 --> 00:00:47.080
they wouldn't have been able to make if they'd
taken a role in the MCU, and it's possible

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:50.670
that Reeves has had this on his mind whenever
Marvel approaches him about a role.

00:00:50.670 --> 00:00:55.289
In this case, it's likely that Reeves' reluctance
to join the MCU is less about what Marvel

00:00:55.289 --> 00:00:59.620
is offering him, and more about the roles
and opportunities he could be forced to give up.

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:03.600
One such role could be the third installment
in the Bill &amp; Ted franchise.

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:08.260
Although Bill &amp; Ted Face the Music is currently
filming, a third movie in the beloved '80s

00:01:08.270 --> 00:01:10.940
franchise has been on Reeves' to-do list for
"a long time."

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:12.540
"Excellent!"

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:17.840
Since at least 2010, Reeves has been openly
discussing his hopes of making a Bill &amp; Ted

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:20.760
threequel, but the film has taken years to
get off the ground.

00:01:20.760 --> 00:01:25.380
And even once the movie finally looked as
though it might finally move into production,

00:01:25.380 --> 00:01:27.580
the journey hasn't been without its obstacles,

00:01:27.760 --> 00:01:30.960
particularly in the financing and creative rights department.

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:35.380
With Bill &amp; Ted 3 on such shaky ground, Reeves
may have been reluctant to make a commitment

00:01:35.390 --> 00:01:39.040
to Marvel that would have made Face the Music
even harder to schedule.

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:42.950
If making this movie was indeed such a high
priority for him, it makes sense that he wouldn't

00:01:42.950 --> 00:01:46.951
have wanted to hand over such a large chunk
of his time and energy to Marvel before it

00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:47.740
was finalized.

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:52.720
No one expected the first John Wick movie
to spawn such a successful franchise, least

00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:53.920
of all Keanu Reeves.

00:01:53.920 --> 00:01:58.200
When Reeves and Chad Stahelski were initially
shopping around the script for the first film,

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:01.520
they were given a hard no by pretty much every
studio in Hollywood.

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:05.460
When they finally did get to make the movie,
it was done on a relatively tight budget of

00:02:05.460 --> 00:02:06.700
$20 million.

00:02:06.700 --> 00:02:11.060
Many of the artistic choices in John Wick,
including the long takes and close-up combat,

00:02:11.070 --> 00:02:15.480
were made due to budget constraints, as the
production couldn't afford multiple cameras

00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:16.760
or fancy editing.

00:02:16.760 --> 00:02:21.600
But despite low expectations, John Wick went
on to be successful enough to justify two

00:02:21.610 --> 00:02:23.460
sequels, with another on the way.

00:02:23.460 --> 00:02:27.890
The Bill &amp; Ted and Matrix films aside, Reeves
isn't typically a franchise actor, and the

00:02:27.890 --> 00:02:32.100
only other movie he's worked on since the
birth of the MCU that hasn't been a standalone

00:02:32.100 --> 00:02:33.460
was Toy Story 4.

00:02:33.460 --> 00:02:36.220
Of course, John Wick wasn't intended to be
any different.

00:02:36.220 --> 00:02:40.200
But considering the runaway success of the
John Wick films and Reeves' ongoing involvement

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:44.450
as the titular assassin, Reeves may not want
to sign up for another major film franchise

00:02:44.450 --> 00:02:46.840
until he wraps up the franchise he's already
in.

00:02:46.840 --> 00:02:51.070
In fact, that's exactly why he turned down
the part of Yon-Rogg in Captain Marvel, because

00:02:51.070 --> 00:02:52.740
he had to work on John Wick 3.

00:02:52.740 --> 00:02:57.310
So the bad guy part went to Jude Law instead,
and Reeves remained tantalizingly out of reach

00:02:57.310 --> 00:02:58.860
for the Marvel Cinematic Universe.

00:02:59.500 --> 00:03:04.010
In a surprising development that practically
no one saw coming, Variety broke the story

00:03:04.010 --> 00:03:09.670
in August 2019 that, 16 years after The Matrix:
Revolutions seemingly concluded the Matrix

00:03:09.670 --> 00:03:14.450
trilogy, Reeves and co-star Carrie-Anne Moss
would be reuniting with director Lana Wachowski

00:03:14.450 --> 00:03:16.420
to shoot a fourth Matrix film.

00:03:16.680 --> 00:03:17.440
"Whoa."

00:03:17.720 --> 00:03:21.960
This film will be helmed only by Lana, without
her sister Lilly, with whom she co-directed

00:03:21.960 --> 00:03:23.520
the first three Matrix films.

00:03:23.520 --> 00:03:27.750
Rumors of a new Matrix movie have been swirling
around for a few years, but most signs seemed

00:03:27.750 --> 00:03:32.340
to point to a reboot of the popular franchise
centering a new character, not a sequel with

00:03:32.340 --> 00:03:33.459
the original cast.

00:03:33.459 --> 00:03:37.930
However, now it's clear that Wachowski's script
will once again follow Reeves' and Moss' characters

00:03:37.930 --> 00:03:42.150
Neo and Trinity, it makes sense that Reeves
would want to keep his schedule wide open.

00:03:42.150 --> 00:03:47.380
With production now slated to ramp up in 2020,
the new Matrix film will keep Reeves occupied

00:03:47.380 --> 00:03:51.990
well into Phase 4 of the MCU, which may explain
why he hasn't been eager to jump on board

00:03:51.990 --> 00:03:53.360
the Marvel train just yet.

00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:57.600
But it's not just his long slate of upcoming
projects that could be keeping Reeves too

00:03:57.600 --> 00:03:59.380
busy to enter the MCU.

00:03:59.380 --> 00:04:03.780
Reeves is a man of many interests and talents,
and he's dabbled in a variety of professions

00:04:03.790 --> 00:04:04.790
throughout the years.

00:04:04.790 --> 00:04:10.100
In 2011, when the MCU was first gathering
steam, Keanu was starting the Arch Motorcycle Company.

00:04:10.300 --> 00:04:15.000
Reeves has been a diehard motorcycle enthusiast
for over three decades, with an extensive

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:19.400
personal collection of much-loved bikes that
he's carefully curated over the years.

00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:24.180
Arch allows him to feed his passion for motorcycles,
creating custom high-end bikes that can carry

00:04:24.180 --> 00:04:29.800
price tags of over $120,000, and which Reeves
is clearly tremendously proud of.

00:04:29.800 --> 00:04:34.420
Outside of acting and motorcycles, Reeves
has also played bass in the band Dogstar,

00:04:34.430 --> 00:04:38.800
written and published books with artist Alexandra
Grant, and produced a number of films.

00:04:38.800 --> 00:04:43.180
Now, it's not unheard of for MCU actors to
carve out time to pursue other endeavors,

00:04:43.180 --> 00:04:47.960
just look at Jeremy Renner's singing career
and Mark Ruffalo's tireless work against climate change.

00:04:47.960 --> 00:04:52.700
But it can't be easy to balance outside interests
with the strenuous demands of an MCU contract.

00:04:52.900 --> 00:04:56.860
With so many irons in the fire, Reeves may
enjoy the freedom of not being locked into

00:04:56.860 --> 00:04:58.520
a multi-year Marvel contract.

00:04:58.520 --> 00:05:02.980
Even if he's still able to squeeze everything
in around any potential superhero gig, the

00:05:02.980 --> 00:05:06.800
stress of juggling them all may make it difficult
to actually enjoy any of them.

00:05:06.800 --> 00:05:10.320
And if you're not enjoying your passion projects,
what's the point of doing them at all?

00:05:10.880 --> 00:05:15.620
Beyond the demands of their long contracts,
MCU actors also live under constant and relentless

00:05:15.620 --> 00:05:16.720
public scrutiny.

00:05:16.720 --> 00:05:21.340
In addition to starring in the movies themselves,
they're expected to engage in extensive promotion

00:05:21.340 --> 00:05:26.130
for Marvel's films, answering the same questions
over and over for a never-ending parade of

00:05:26.130 --> 00:05:27.930
journalists and talk show hosts.

00:05:27.930 --> 00:05:32.139
And while Reeves is an A-list star already,
the notoriously private and introverted actor

00:05:32.139 --> 00:05:36.210
may be daunted by the idea of throwing himself
into the MCU limelight.

00:05:36.210 --> 00:05:40.660
Speaking about Reeves to GQ, John Wick Chapter
2 actor Peter Stormare has said:

00:05:40.660 --> 00:05:44.540
"He's a loner...They think he's putting on
some kind of a fake face, when he's stuttering,

00:05:44.540 --> 00:05:47.880
giving interviews on the red carpet, and he
looks away and looks uncomfortable.

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:48.820
But he really is."

00:05:48.820 --> 00:05:53.271
Considering just how many red carpets Marvel
actors have to walk, it's possible that Reeves

00:05:53.271 --> 00:05:57.830
has decided that being a part of the MCU just
isn't worth being forced to spend so much

00:05:57.830 --> 00:05:59.320
time in the public eye.

00:05:59.920 --> 00:06:03.820
Due to Marvel's reliance on returning cast
members and their movies' demanding production

00:06:03.820 --> 00:06:08.640
schedule, the studio has never been particularly
eager to take risks when it comes to its stars.

00:06:08.640 --> 00:06:13.060
Not only could injury-induced production delays
throw their entire multi-year plan off track,

00:06:13.060 --> 00:06:16.660
but the cost of insuring its A-list stars
while they perform their own stunts would

00:06:16.670 --> 00:06:18.040
be astronomical.

00:06:18.040 --> 00:06:21.680
Because of this, Marvel actors are contractually
prohibited from doing the bulk of their own

00:06:21.680 --> 00:06:22.280
stunt work.

00:06:22.400 --> 00:06:26.100
But Reeves is known for doing most of his
own stunts, and may indeed be turned off by

00:06:26.100 --> 00:06:27.770
Marvel's hardline policy.

00:06:27.770 --> 00:06:32.740
Speaking about John Wick: Chapter 3, director
and former Reeves stunt double Chad Stahelski

00:06:32.740 --> 00:06:33.740
told GQ:

00:06:33.740 --> 00:06:38.590
"If you've got an actor who can ride horses,
ride motorcycles, do fight scenes, why not?

00:06:38.590 --> 00:06:43.479
I made a list of every skill Keanu has, we
sat down and I said, 'Give me everything you

00:06:43.479 --> 00:06:44.600
can do really well.'

00:06:44.600 --> 00:06:46.050
And we put all that in the movies."

00:06:46.050 --> 00:06:49.720
Now that he's accustomed to action movies
that play to his physical strengths and allow

00:06:49.720 --> 00:06:54.230
him to showcase his considerable action skills,
it wouldn't be surprising if being hamstrung

00:06:54.230 --> 00:06:57.440
by a studio contract seems less than appealing
to Reeves.

00:06:57.440 --> 00:07:01.200
Then there's the chance that Marvel has been
offering him roles that aren't exactly super physical

00:07:01.200 --> 00:07:05.500
For example, Reeves may have made a great
Collector, Everett K. Ross, or even Stephen

00:07:05.500 --> 00:07:09.199
Strange, but none of those roles would've
tapped into the sort of physicality the actor

00:07:09.200 --> 00:07:10.160
is known for.

00:07:10.160 --> 00:07:14.080
After all, it would be a bit of a letdown,
for both the audience and for Reeves himself,

00:07:14.100 --> 00:07:18.580
if the actor known for doing 90 percent of
his action scenes in stunt-heavy movies finally

00:07:18.580 --> 00:07:22.830
took a role in the MCU, and ended up just
standing there and waving his hands for most

00:07:22.830 --> 00:07:23.400
of the time.

00:07:24.120 --> 00:07:27.680
Being the huge fan of comic books that he
is, there's a good chance that the reason

00:07:27.690 --> 00:07:31.639
Reeves has been reluctant to take a role in
the MCU is because he's holding out for the

00:07:31.639 --> 00:07:33.770
chance to play one specific character.

00:07:33.770 --> 00:07:38.220
In fact, there are a number of roles within
the Marvel universe that Reeves would be well-suited to play.

00:07:38.440 --> 00:07:42.680
Adam Warlock, the perfect being teased at
the end of Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 2,

00:07:42.700 --> 00:07:47.020
could be a good fit for Reeves, who, let's
face it, is often rumored to be perfect himself.

00:07:47.020 --> 00:07:50.460
Another option might be Reed Richards, the
leader of the Fantastic Four.

00:07:50.460 --> 00:07:54.820
Disney recently reclaimed the Fantastic Four
from Fox, and with Tony Stark gone after the

00:07:54.820 --> 00:07:59.410
events of Avengers: Endgame, the MCU has a
space open for a new scientist hero.

00:07:59.410 --> 00:08:03.700
Along with the Fantastic Four comes the alien
antagonist-turned-ally Silver Surfer, who

00:08:03.700 --> 00:08:05.910
could also provide a meaty role for Reeves.

00:08:05.910 --> 00:08:09.880
Or maybe Reeves wants to play Ghost Rider,
a character that he's always been a fan of,

00:08:09.880 --> 00:08:13.600
and one that would allow him to bring his
love of motorcycles to the MCU.

00:08:13.600 --> 00:08:17.380
While this character was already introduced
in the TV series Marvel's Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D.,

00:08:17.380 --> 00:08:21.700
it wouldn't be a huge surprise if the character
was recast for the big screen, especially

00:08:21.700 --> 00:08:24.930
if Marvel could pull in an actor of Reeves'
caliber to play him.

00:08:24.930 --> 00:08:29.190
Keanu Reeves has also told MTV in the past
that one of his favorite comic stories is

00:08:29.190 --> 00:08:31.110
Frank Miller's run of Wolverine.

00:08:31.110 --> 00:08:35.179
Due to Marvel's sale of the rights to the
X-Men to Fox in the '90s, mutants have never

00:08:35.179 --> 00:08:37.269
appeared in the MCU so far.

00:08:37.269 --> 00:08:40.550
That may be about to change with Disney's
recent acquisition of Fox.

00:08:40.550 --> 00:08:45.190
At San Diego Comic Con in 2019, Kevin Feige
recently hinted that mutants were indeed on

00:08:45.190 --> 00:08:49.850
the horizon for the MCU, which may be exactly
what Reeves has been waiting for.

00:08:49.850 --> 00:08:50.850
Reeves told MTV:

00:08:50.850 --> 00:08:52.180
"I always wanted to play Wolverine.

00:08:52.180 --> 00:08:53.480
I missed that one."

00:08:53.480 --> 00:08:57.829
With mutants now finally headed to the MCU,
Reeves may finally get his chance to sport

00:08:57.829 --> 00:08:59.380
a set of adamantium claws.

00:09:00.680 --> 00:09:04.990
At the end of the day, however, the MCU may
just have nothing to offer Keanu Reeves, a

00:09:04.990 --> 00:09:08.660
man who is already one of the most beloved
actors in Hollywood, who cares very little

00:09:08.660 --> 00:09:13.119
about money, and who is, by all accounts,
a genuinely good person who frequently goes

00:09:13.119 --> 00:09:15.929
out of his way to make the world a better
place for others.

00:09:15.929 --> 00:09:22.889
"The feeling of being there, of walking the
streets of the future, is really going to

00:09:22.889 --> 00:09:24.059
be breathtaking."

00:09:24.060 --> 00:09:25.740
"You're breathtaking!"

00:09:25.900 --> 00:09:30.600
Acting in the MCU can give a huge boost to
an actor's career, catapulting them from relative

00:09:30.600 --> 00:09:34.689
unknowns to some of the most sought-after
names in Hollywood practically overnight.

00:09:34.689 --> 00:09:38.329
But for an actor like Reeves, who is already
a household name with enough star power to

00:09:38.329 --> 00:09:42.319
pursue pretty much any project he wants to
make, that may not be much of an incentive

00:09:42.320 --> 00:09:45.360
to sign up for a decade-long contract with
Marvel.

00:09:45.360 --> 00:09:50.079
Similarly, Reeves doesn't exactly need the
MCU to endear him to the many fans who already

00:09:50.080 --> 00:09:50.800
love him.

00:09:50.800 --> 00:09:55.160
Marvel actors are expected to be heroes both
off and on the big screen, but Reeves doesn't

00:09:55.170 --> 00:09:59.860
exactly need a studio contract to prompt him
to be generous and kind, and he's consistently

00:09:59.860 --> 00:10:04.100
reported to be among the nicest people anyone
could ever have the pleasure of meeting.

00:10:04.100 --> 00:10:05.660
"You're breathtaking!

00:10:06.280 --> 00:10:08.300
You're all breathtaking!"

00:10:08.740 --> 00:10:13.060
And that's the crux of it: why play a superhero
when you're already one in real life?

